{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Gary Lewis & The Playboys and Eagles fit my interest in revisiting older hits, reflected in AM Gold: The Mid-'60s and Now Classic Rock Hits.",
    "Bread connects with the gentler listening mood I associate with Simon & Garfunkel, while Neil Diamond offers the familiar older pop songs I want right now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Adele 21 does not connect as strongly with my current wish to revisit older favorites; having listened to Born This Way does not mean I want more contemporary pop today.",
    "Titles such as 25, Partners, and Title give me too little information to connect them with my listening interests, so I would pass rather than assume they fit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My occasional interest in newer pop seems to have been taken as a stronger guide to today's choices than it is.",
    "Greatest-hits collections appeal to me, but that does not mean I want several overlapping collections from the same artist in one visit."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The repeated older hits collections in my history matter because I want familiar songs from that period, not simply any release described as a collection.",
    "Interest does not always mean I would choose something now: I would save the Bee Gees for later and choose only one Neil Diamond collection this time."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations mostly understood my interest in familiar older hits, but gave too much weight to occasional newer pop listening and repeated collections."
}"}
